    "content": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud arrived in the southern, Galmudug-controlled section of Galkayo on Monday, a city that has recently witnessed violent confrontations between his troops and those loyal to Puntland. His visit comes despite a public warning from Puntland officials, who had advised against the trip. Puntland's President, Saeed Abdullahi Deni, remains in the northern part of the city, which is under his administration's control, just a few kilometers away.\n\nThe visit occurs against the backdrop of recent clashes in Galkayo, where forces allied with President Mohamud suffered a heavy defeat. The fighting highlights the ongoing political and military tensions between the federal government and Puntland, which has been seeking greater autonomy. The two leaders have been at odds over various issues, including the control of territories and the distribution of resources.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this visit underscores the fragile nature of peace in the region and the persistent challenges to national unity. Many diaspora members have family and business interests in Galkayo, and any instability can have direct consequences on their livelihoods and their ability to maintain ties with their homeland. The visit also signals the federal government's determination to assert its presence in contested areas, even as Puntland pushes back.\n\nThe situation in Galkayo remains delicate, with both leaders present in close proximity. Observers will be watching closely to see if this visit leads to dialogue or further confrontation. The international community, including Somali diaspora organizations, has previously called for peaceful resolution of disputes between the federal government and federal member states.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/somalia-president-defies-puntland-warning-visits-galkayo/",
